      "alt": "Infographic titled \"Nearness and parallel work\" detailing a 3-step process for agent coordination:\nStep 1: Identify each agent's active changes\nCompares two agents (Agent A and Agent B) showing icons for base commit, changed file, and changed function. Net changes are tracked since base commit plus dirty edits and new files, mapping changed lines to files and functions.\nStep 2: Estimate interaction risk\nLists four risk categories:\n * Edit overlap: Changes touch the same code.\n * Dependency impact: One change alters a contract another relies on.\n * Historical coupling: Files change together more often than chance.\n * CI evidence: Past combined changes failed; repairs reveal why.\nA summary box defines \"Nearness = estimated need for coordination\" by weighting evidence by confidence and recency.\nStep 3: Coordinate only where needed\nShows diagrammed workflows for pairs of agents:\n * Negotiate: Agent pairs A-B and C-D have active communication links.\n * Independent: Agent pairs E-F and G-H work independently in separate lanes.\nExplanatory text notes to connect agents whose changes are likely to interact, while independent work adds parallel lanes without joining a global queue, recalculated as edits, negotiations, and CI results change.\n",
