      "alt": "The new tests cover 320 combinations of storage layout, bit order, polarity, and image size, plus every possible byte pattern. I’m also adding an upstream 1-bit image and packed fixtures to the mutation-fuzzing corpus.\n\n[Icon] Inspected TIFF artifacts, fixed tile reads, and verified documentation\n\nThe Rust output matches the expected pixels. The comparison tests exposed a libtiff 4.7.1 issue with small, LSB-first tiles: its RGBA reader checks allocated buffer capacity against tile size. I’ve adjusted the test oracle to supply an exact-size buffer through libtiff’s public API; libtiff still performs all decoding.\n\n[Icon] Inspecting Logs and Verification Code",
